        <p>KITCHENER'S ARMY. ARTILLERY BRIGADES TO BE FORMED. RECRUITS WANTED HERE AND NOW. LORD DERBY has been requested by Lord Kitchener to raise in West Lancashire, two Brigades of Field Artillery, with their attendant Ammu- nition Column, and a Battery of Heavy Artillery. PAY AND ALLOWANCE AS IN REGULAR ARMY. Smart men, especially those who have previous Artillery experience—or who can ride -are particularly invited to come forward. Care will be taken to, as far as possible, keep friends together. Come Forward and form 'Comrades' Artillery Brigades. The men will he billeted for the present at Lytham for training. Recruits will' be taken at COOPER'S BUILDINGS, CHURCH ST., LIVERPOOL,. or at any Local Recruiting Office, starting MONDAY NEXT, February Bth, at 9 o'clock. Office open each day afterwards.</p>
