        <p>TO-DAY'S YORKSHIRE VISITORS. Warrington Meet Dewsbury for the First Time This Season. Warrington meet Dewsbury this afternoon for the first time this seastin, the Wilderspool ground being the venue of the encounter. Warrington hope to field a good side, the fol- lowing having been selected to represent them: Warrington. 1 B. Jolley. 2 Baker, 3 Tranter, 4 Brookes (capt.), 5 Bradshaw. 6 Laws, 7 Young. 8 Cox, 9 Fearnley, 10 Mather, 11 Green, 12 W. Cunliffe, 13 T.,Curdiffe. /- Dewsbury's team will be selected frqpi the following 16 players: 1 W. Stringer. • 5 Ed. Ward, 3 W. Rhodes, 4 T. Price, 16 Ernest Ward, and 2 L. Farrar. 6 E. Rogers, 7 W. Dyson. 10 P. Brown, 9 W. Bradford, 8 F. Watkinson, 11 A. V. Abbishaw, 12 R. Robertshaw, 15 A. J. Thomas, .13 F. Gallagher, 14 J. Kilcommon. The kick-off is timed for 3. o'clock, and the officials in charge of the match will be: Referee, Mr. R. Wailing (Widnes) touch-judges, Messrs. F. Fairhurst (Wigan) and T. Kiley (Leigh). SALFORD CHALLENGE SHIELD. First Round. Rylands' Recs. v. Bradford and Clayton. At Gorsey-lane to-day; kick-off 3 p.m. ; - Rylands': F. Horrocks; J. Griffiths, F. Pot:- ter, C. Povey, and A. Rowlinson ; J. Gallop and A. Horrocks; J. ,Brandwood, W. Shaw,,F. Bagu- ley, J. Dumbell, A. Penn, and A. N. Other. INTERMEDIATE RUGBY LEAGUE. LAST SATURDAY'S RESULTS. Sacred Heart 0.8., 14 points; Wycliffe, 3. Arpley-street 0.8., 18; St. James' Juniors, 0. TO-DAY'S MATCHES. Parochial, 0.8. v. St. Barnabas 0.B.; referee, Mr. Crozier.' St. James' 0.8. v. Beamont United; Mr. Jones Bolton. C. 0.8. v. Beamont Ath.; Mr. Wil- liams.</p>
